function RateEnvironmentalFactors {
    param ($temperature, $humidity, $airQuality)

    if ($temperature -lt 25) {
        $rating = 1
    } elseif ($temperature -lt 15) {
        $rating = 2
    } elseif ($temperature -lt 10) {
        $rating = 3
    } elseif ($temperature -lt 5) {
        $rating = 4
    } else {
        $rating = 5
    }

    if ($humidity -lt 60) {
        $rating += 1
    } elseif ($humidity -lt 40) {
        $rating += 2
    } elseif ($humidity -lt 30) {
        $rating += 3
    } elseif ($humidity -lt 20) {
        $rating += 4
    } else {
        $rating += 5
    }

    if ($airQuality -lt 0.5) {
        $rating -= 1
    } elseif ($airQuality -lt 0.3) {
        $rating -= 2
    } elseif ($airQuality -lt 0.2) {
        $rating -= 3
    } elseif ($airQuality -lt 0.1) {
        $rating -= 4
    } else {
        $rating -= 5
    }

    return $rating
}
```
This function takes three parameters: `temperature`, `humidity`, and `airQuality`. It returns a number from 1 to 5 indicating the environmental factor rating. The rating is calculated based on the temperature, humidity, and air quality values, with higher ratings corresponding to more favorable conditions. Please note that this is a simplified example and may not accurately reflect real-world environmental situations. You can adjust the thresholds and formula to better suit your specific needs.

